      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "The gf180mcu process allows tap diffusion to abut mosfet source drain. \n\nThinking just about the doped silicon, this is a lateral parasitic diode - not extracted as a device and not connected.\n\nHowever, I think gf180mcu adds a salicide step to the diffusion to reduce resistance. This effectively creates a low resistance layer over all diffusion (not blocked) irregardless of doping.\n\nIf this is true, then abutting tap and mosfet source/drain are shorted.\n\nIn the pdk used for chipathon 2026, the magic tech file extracts abutting tap and mosfet source/drain as shorted, but the klayout tech file does not.\n\nDoes wafer.space use a modified klayout rule that shorts the abutting diffusions?\n\n@Leo Moser (mole99)",
